1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,178
Ravi is opening a second Chai
Corner, near the bus stand.

2
00:00:04,478 --> 00:00:06,434
But one stall nearly broke him.

3
00:00:06,434 --> 00:00:07,837
How will he run two?

4
00:00:08,387 --> 00:00:10,450
His to-do list is a mess.

5
00:00:10,450 --> 00:00:11,623
Rent a shop.

6
00:00:11,623 --> 00:00:12,729
Hire people.

7
00:00:12,729 --> 00:00:13,777
Buy stoves.

8
00:00:14,077 --> 00:00:17,235
He jumps from job to job,
and finishes nothing.

9
00:00:17,535 --> 00:00:19,761
And opening day is two weeks away.

10
00:00:20,411 --> 00:00:22,278
Ravi doesn't need more jobs.

11
00:00:22,278 --> 00:00:24,047
He needs the right order.

12
00:00:24,747 --> 00:00:27,070
So, what are the functions of management?

13
00:00:27,370 --> 00:00:31,607
They are the core jobs every manager
does, in every business, again and

14
00:00:31,607 --> 00:00:32,507
again.

15
00:00:32,771 --> 00:00:36,512
In 1937, Luther Gulick
listed seven of them.

16
00:00:36,812 --> 00:00:41,280
Planning, organizing, staffing,
directing, coordinating, reporting, and

17
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:42,180
budgeting.

18
00:00:42,413 --> 00:00:45,210
His list became famous
by its first letters.

19
00:00:45,810 --> 00:00:48,725
Today, most books use
a shorter list of five.

20
00:00:49,075 --> 00:00:51,948
Reporting and budgeting
fold into controlling.

21
00:00:51,948 --> 00:00:54,219
Coordinating runs through them all.

22
00:00:54,869 --> 00:00:57,661
Each function answers one simple question.

23
00:00:58,111 --> 00:01:00,323
Planning asks, what should we do?

24
00:01:00,323 --> 00:01:01,579
Ravi sets a goal.

25
00:01:01,579 --> 00:01:03,172
Two hundred cups a day.

26
00:01:03,522 --> 00:01:05,413
Organizing asks, who does what?

27
00:01:05,413 --> 00:01:08,627
He splits the work into
kitchen, counter, and cleaning.

28
00:01:08,977 --> 00:01:10,704
Staffing asks, who exactly?

29
00:01:10,704 --> 00:01:14,328
Meena will run the new outlet,
and two new helpers join her.

30
00:01:14,678 --> 00:01:17,295
Directing asks, how do we guide them?

31
00:01:17,295 --> 00:01:19,861
Asha trains the helpers on her recipe.

32
00:01:20,211 --> 00:01:22,708
And controlling asks, are we on track?

33
00:01:22,708 --> 00:01:24,961
Kabir counts the cups every evening.

34
00:01:24,961 --> 00:01:26,737
Only one hundred and fifty.

35
00:01:27,387 --> 00:01:29,378
So Ravi goes back to planning.

36
00:01:29,728 --> 00:01:30,646
A new plan.

37
00:01:30,646 --> 00:01:33,288
Open at seven, for the morning commuters.

38
00:01:33,638 --> 00:01:36,765
That's why the five functions
are a cycle, not a list.

39
00:01:37,415 --> 00:01:40,279
One more thing holds the cycle together.

40
00:01:40,279 --> 00:01:41,308
Coordination.

41
00:01:41,608 --> 00:01:45,973
Coordination means making every part
work together, at the right time.

42
00:01:46,323 --> 00:01:50,325
If the helpers start before the stoves
arrive, they have nothing to do.

43
00:01:50,675 --> 00:01:52,328
So Ravi lines them up.

44
00:01:52,328 --> 00:01:55,113
Stoves on day nine, helpers on day ten.

45
00:01:55,463 --> 00:01:58,769
Experts call coordination
the essence of management.

46
00:01:58,769 --> 00:02:00,892
It lives inside every function.

47
00:02:01,542 --> 00:02:05,962
Four weeks later, the new outlet
sells two hundred and ten cups a day.

48
00:02:05,962 --> 00:02:06,877
Goal beaten.

49
00:02:07,527 --> 00:02:11,672
Over the next five episodes, we'll
take these functions one at a time.

50
00:02:12,322 --> 00:02:13,249
Quick check.

51
00:02:13,249 --> 00:02:16,987
Ravi picks Meena to run the
outlet, and hires two helpers.

52
00:02:16,987 --> 00:02:18,555
Which function is this?

53
00:02:20,455 --> 00:02:21,355
Staffing!

54
00:02:21,233 --> 00:02:24,133
It answers who exactly will fill each job.

55
00:02:24,733 --> 00:02:25,746
So, remember.

56
00:02:26,046 --> 00:02:30,897
The five functions are planning, organizing,
staffing, directing, and controlling.

57
00:02:31,247 --> 00:02:32,718
They work as a cycle.

58
00:02:32,718 --> 00:02:34,832
Controlling leads back to planning.

59
00:02:35,182 --> 00:02:37,863
And coordination ties them all together.

60
00:02:38,463 --> 00:02:42,506
Next time, we'll zoom into the first
function, planning, and how to set

61
00:02:42,506 --> 00:02:43,406
good goals.
